  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "these facts is, that Paras'urâma had not been honoured with the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "\" relatio inter divos\" in the time of Kâlidâsa, while he had been",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "so honoured in the time of Bhartṛihari. If so, Bhartṛihari was",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "most probably much later in age than Kâlidâsa.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Right margin is obscured/darkened, and cut-outs miss parts of lines."
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Thus far the observations which I have already made else-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "where on this topic. We shall now proceed a step further.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Tradition informs us, as already remarked, that Bhartṛihari was a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "brother of king Vikrama, and that besides the S'atakas he com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "posed a work called the Vâkyapadîya or Vâkyapradîpa. Now",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "it is well known, that this Vikrama is popularly believed to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "identical with the Founder of the Samvat Era, and to have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "flourished about 56 B. C.[*] But it seems to me quite im-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "possible to accept this date as the date of Bhartṛihari and this",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "for the following reasons:—The Vâkyapadîya shows very clear-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "ly that its author lived at least one generation after the Chan-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "drâchârya and others who brought the great commentary of Pa-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "tanjali into general use after it had for some time remained in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "obscurity.[†] Now if we accept Prof. Weber's opinion about the",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Right margin is obscured/darkened, and cut-outs miss parts of lines."
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "* Bohlen who accepts the identity of the Bhartṛihari of the S'atakas",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "and the Hari of the Vâkyapadîya (Præfatio p. vi.) is of a different opi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "nion. Speaking of this date, viz. 56 B. C., he says \"quo de temporis",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "momento nulla sane dubitandi causa adest idonea.\" On the contrary we",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "contend, as in the text, that there is such a causa idonea and not merely",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "a causa but causæ. Of course if the identity of the grammarian Bhartṛi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "hari and the poet Bhartṛihari be disproved, the arguments we have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "based on that identity will at once fall to the ground. But then, while",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "one part of the tradition turns out to be unbelievable, the other part",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "will not be entitled to much credence, and thus the ground will still be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "cut off from under the only opposing argument for the contemporaneity",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "of Vikrama and Bhartṛihari. And the question will then be left open.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "Colebrooke (Essays Vol. II., p. 6.) also does not question this date.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Right margin is obscured/darkened, and cut-outs miss parts of lines."
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "† See the interesting account of this matter in Siddh. Kaumudî",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "(Introduction by Târânâth) also Goldstücker's Pâṇini ad finem. Weber",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "also in his Review of the latter work seems to have discussed this mat-",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": true,
      "note": "Right margin is obscured/darkened; line 4 of the footnote on the page ('ter (see Indian Antiquary Vol. II. p. 206).') was excluded from the region cut-out."
    },
